// Negative fixture: a non-literal size on an *inner* array dimension is a
// semantic error - ir.py's _gen_array_declare only recovers one
// runtime-computed size expression (the outermost), so a dynamic size
// anywhere else has nowhere to go. Only the outermost dimension (the last
// bracket written, e.g. `arr[n];`) may be non-literal - see
// tests/dynamic_array.src for that supported case.
int f(int n) {
    var int grid[n][3];
    return grid[0][0];
}

void main() {
    print(f(3));
}
